    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Signalized intersections typically struggle with peak hour throughput compared to roundabouts. During peak hours, traffic lights can cause greater queueing delays as the flow is regulated separately for each incoming lane or direction. Signalized intersections also experience more system friction due to the start-stop nature of traffic lights. In contrast, roundabouts generally handle higher throughput and reduce queueing delays during peak hours by continuously moving traffic, minimizing stops. As a result, roundabouts usually have lower system friction, improving overall traffic flow.",
